Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and how they will be used  
• `trip_seconds`: to calculate the trip duration (in seconds), filter to 0‑–60 minutes, build the quantiles and report min/max duration.  
• `fare`: to calculate the average fare for every quantile group.  
• `unique_key`: only for possible counting / identification of records (not strictly necessary for the final result, but useful while exploring).  

Filters / conditions that will be applied  
• `trip_seconds > 0` – exclude zero‑length or negative records.  
• `trip_seconds <= 3600` – keep only trips that lasted 60 minutes (3600 seconds) or less.  

Below are 10 BigQuery SQL queries, starting from very simple inspections and gradually building up to the final answer.  
(Replace nothing – the full table names are already used. Each exploration query is limited to 20 rows; the final query has no limit.)

```sql
-- 1) Quick look at raw trip‑duration and fare values
SELECT trip_seconds, fare
FROM `bigquery-public-data.chicago_taxi_trips.taxi_trips`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Distinct payment types just to understand the data vocabulary
SELECT DISTINCT payment_type
FROM `bigquery-public-data.chicago_taxi_trips.taxi_trips`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Sample of trips whose duration is between 0 and 60 minutes
SELECT unique_key, trip_seconds, fare
FROM `bigquery-public-data.chicago_taxi_trips.taxi_trips`
WHERE trip_seconds > 0
  AND trip_seconds <= 3600
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Same sample, adding duration in minutes (rounded)
SELECT unique_key,
       trip_seconds,
       ROUND(trip_seconds / 60.0) AS trip_minutes_rounded,
       fare
FROM `bigquery-public-data.chicago_taxi_trips.taxi_trips`
WHERE trip_seconds > 0
  AND trip_seconds <= 3600
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Approximate boundaries of six equal quantiles (hexiles) of trip length
SELECT APPROX_QUANTILES(trip_seconds, 6) AS sec_quantile_boundaries
FROM `bigquery-public-data.chicago_taxi_trips.taxi_trips`
WHERE trip_seconds > 0
  AND trip_seconds <= 3600;
```

```sql
-- 6) Attach a hexile index (1‑6) to each qualifying trip
SELECT unique_key,
       trip_seconds,
       NTILE(6) OVER (ORDER BY trip_seconds) AS duration_hexile
FROM `bigquery-public-data.chicago_taxi_trips.taxi_trips`
WHERE trip_seconds > 0
  AND trip_seconds <= 3600
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Inspect one of those hexile buckets (example: bucket 3)
WITH ranked AS (
  SELECT unique_key,
         trip_seconds,
         fare,
         NTILE(6) OVER (ORDER BY trip_seconds) AS duration_hexile
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.chicago_taxi_trips.taxi_trips`
  WHERE trip_seconds > 0
    AND trip_seconds <= 3600
)
SELECT *
FROM ranked
WHERE duration_hexile = 3
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Aggregate min/max trip_minutes (rounded) and trip count per hexile
WITH ranked AS (
  SELECT trip_seconds,
         NTILE(6) OVER (ORDER BY trip_seconds) AS duration_hexile
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.chicago_taxi_trips.taxi_trips`
  WHERE trip_seconds > 0
    AND trip_seconds <= 3600
)
SELECT duration_hexile,
       MIN(ROUND(trip_seconds / 60.0)) AS min_minute,
       MAX(ROUND(trip_seconds / 60.0)) AS max_minute,
       COUNT(*)                    AS trip_cnt
FROM ranked
GROUP BY duration_hexile
ORDER BY duration_hexile
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9) Same aggregate, adding average fare
WITH ranked AS (
  SELECT trip_seconds,
         fare,
         NTILE(6) OVER (ORDER BY trip_seconds) AS duration_hexile
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.chicago_taxi_trips.taxi_trips`
  WHERE trip_seconds > 0
    AND trip_seconds <= 3600
)
SELECT duration_hexile,
       MIN(ROUND(trip_seconds / 60.0)) AS min_minute,
       MAX(ROUND(trip_seconds / 60.0)) AS max_minute,
       COUNT(*)                        AS trip_cnt,
       AVG(fare)                       AS avg_fare
FROM ranked
GROUP BY duration_hexile
ORDER BY duration_hexile
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10) FINAL ANSWER: six equal‑frequency quantile groups for trips ≤ 60 minutes
WITH filtered AS (
  SELECT trip_seconds, fare
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.chicago_taxi_trips.taxi_trips`
  WHERE trip_seconds > 0
    AND trip_seconds <= 3600            -- 0‑–60 min window
),
ranked AS (
  SELECT trip_seconds,
         fare,
         NTILE(6) OVER (ORDER BY trip_seconds) AS duration_quantile
  FROM filtered
)
SELECT duration_quantile                               AS quantile_group,
       MIN(ROUND(trip_seconds / 60.0)) AS min_duration_minutes,
       MAX(ROUND(trip_seconds / 60.0)) AS max_duration_minutes,
       COUNT(*)                        AS total_trips,
       AVG(fare)                       AS average_fare
FROM ranked
GROUP BY quantile_group
ORDER BY quantile_group;
```

The last query (10) returns, for each of the six equal‑frequency trip‑duration groups (quantiles 1‑6):

• the minimum and maximum duration in whole minutes,  
• the total number of trips in that group, and  
• the average fare.
